{"task":"Merge master's installer TUI, and fix six README defects","goals":"Take the landed TUI, and correct the mode-collapse fallout left in the README","status":"Waiting","recorded_at":"2026-09-10T04:11:16Z","body":"claude/lucid-ember-7451 landed on master (cdb7e3b) while this branch was working, so this\nmerges it in and fixes the six README defects the session that reviewed it reported.\n\nThree conflicts in install.sh, all the same shape and all resolved in master's favour. That\nbranch replaced the installer's prompts with an arrow-key TUI, and `ask` there returns the\nanswer through ANSWER because the prompt is now DRAWN on stdout — the version here was a\ncompatibility shim written two commits ago to keep `$(ask …)` call sites working across the\nmerge. With the real implementation landed the shim has nothing left to do, so master's side\nwins in all three: `ask`, the TLD and sites questions (now edit_tld / edit_sites), and the\nproxy-fallback question, which they had already rebuilt as a menu_select carrying both\nanswers and their consequences. Verified master's install.sh still carries everything from\nthis side — the launchd takedown, job_config, free_port_from, PROXY_FALLBACK, shell_rc — and\nit does.\n\nThe six README defects, all verified present here before fixing and all fallout from work on\nthis branch rather than theirs:\n\n  1. A dead link to templates/Caddyfile.auto.tmpl, renamed to Caddyfile.tmpl when the modes\n     collapsed. Label and href both. The sentence around it calls that file the\n     authoritative description of the routing, so it is the one link a curious reader\n     follows.\n  2. The Contents entry for Updating carried a U+FE0F variation selector inside the href,\n     between the # and the slug, so it resolved to nothing. Removed from the href only; the\n     heading keeps its emoji, and GitHub's slug for it is plain.\n  3. \"In `auto` mode the site is live immediately\" — there are no modes.\n  4. \"Every auto-mode site also answers over plain HTTP\" — same.\n  5. \"(auto mode)\" on the `ldev apply` comment — same.\n  6. \"sudo for three things\" is now four: the resolver file, the local CA, the launchd\n     service, and taking down another launchd job that already holds 80 or 443. The PATH\n     line is a prompt too and was unmentioned, so it is named as the one that needs no sudo.\n\nThe reviewing session proposed splitting these and gave 6 to the installer branch. Taking it\nhere instead: both the takedown and the PATH prompt were added on this branch, so the fourth\nsudo and the missing prompt are both this side's omissions, not theirs.\n\nChecked rather than assumed, since two of the six were broken links: every relative link in\nthe README resolves to a file that exists, and all 18 in-page anchors match a heading under\nGitHub's slug rules. The first pass of that check reported every anchor dead, which was the\nchecker stripping the emoji before the space it sat beside — GitHub keeps the hyphen that\nleaves behind, which is exactly why the entry in defect 2 needed a character removed rather\nthan added.\n\nOne thing NOT fixed, and not this branch's: test/tui-menu.test.sh fails one of its 77\nassertions on master — \"--defaults got as far as the privileged steps\". Confirmed\npre-existing by running it against master's bin/ldev and master's templates with only this\nbranch's tests present: same single failure. Left for the session that owns that test.\n","parent_commit":"be8849ed4c912ce4b78952d051b3955fd462f740","repo":"brave-cedar-fb33","pct":"43","tasks":[{"id":"merge","content":"Merge master (cdb7e3b), resolving the three install.sh conflicts in the TUI's favour","status":"completed"},{"id":"readme","content":"Fix all six reported README defects, including the two broken links","status":"completed"},{"id":"linkcheck","content":"Verify every relative link and all 18 in-page anchors resolve","status":"completed"},{"id":"tui-test","content":"test/tui-menu.test.sh fails one asser